{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control", "label": "ADR 0020: The anchor issue is the brief's access control, and impersonation is deferred", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_anchor_issue_access_control", "label": "The anchor issue is the brief's access control", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Names the mechanism that already exists: the administrator picks the anchor, Jira enforces BROWSE on it at send time. The residual aggregate leak is accepted for ADR 0019's reasons plus one more: a brief recipient has been vouched for twice (administrator and Jira), a panel reader once, so answering this more strictly than the stores would be incoherent."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_offline_user_impersonation_deferred", "label": "Offline user impersonation (asUser(accountId), allowImpersonation) is deferred, not rejected", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ADR 0018 called per-recipient composition 'a different product'; that was written from memory and is wrong \u2014 Forge documents it, with a scheduled trigger as the motivating case. Deferred because an app not on the Marketplace can only impersonate contributors, every send multiplies, and trigger-runtime support is unverified. tests/test_service.py fails if allowImpersonation appears without revisiting this record."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_administer_jira_refused", "label": "Administer Jira global permission refused", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "permissions/check for another user needs it, it is the largest grant discussed anywhere in the repository, and the endpoint's own docs say the answer may not hold for all issues anyway. Refused again in ADR 0021 for reading Jira's audit log."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_what_would_change_the_decision", "label": "Conditions that would revive impersonation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the brief ever names an issue (checked in tests); if a customer runs issue-level security and says so; if the app is distributed through the Marketplace."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control", "target": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_anchor_issue_access_control", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control", "target": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_control_offline_user_impersonation_deferred", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0020-the-anchor-issue-is-the-brief-s-access-control.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0020_the_anchor_issue_is_the_brief_s_access_cont